      "category": "List-item",
      "text": "(f) Every officer and employee of the City School District of the City of New York, including the members of the Board of Education, the Chancellor, all Community School Boards and Community Superintendents, and all other officers and employees of the City shall have the affirmative obligation to report, directly and without undue delay, to the Deputy Commissioner, any and all information concerning conduct which they know or should reasonably know may involve corrupt or other criminal activity or conflict of interest (i) by an officer or employee of the City School District, which concerns his or her office or employment, or (ii) by persons dealing with the City School District, which concerns their dealing with the school district, and shall proceed in accordance with the Deputy Commissioner's directions. The knowing failure of any officer or employee to so report shall constitute cause for removal from office or other appropriate penalty.",
